   "Minifigure assembly (helmet, visor, head, torso, legs) in the yellow box is not in the parts list, so it is not recorded.",
   "Step 2: the black 2x6 plate (379526) is assumed to sit under the rear of the wedge brick, so it rests on nothing and is joined to b1 in other_joins. The two white 1x2 plates and the 2x2 plate are assumed to sit on the wedge top beside the black brick.",
   "Step 3: the 1x4 plate (371001) is assumed to rest on the two 1x2 plates. The two inverted sloped bricks (4259937) are assumed to be skids on the 2x6 plate.",
   "Step 4: the hinge sub-assembly is white Technic brick, then black hinge base, then white hinge top plate. The final picture shows black studs on top, so the hinge top's attachment is uncertain. It is placed on the 1x4 plate. The two trans-dark-blue round plates sit on the skid ends.",
   "The booklet picture is low resolution, so exact stud contacts are best guesses.",
   "Page 2 shows steps 5 and 6. The lower half of the page is an advertisement for other sets (7235, 7236, 7237, 7245) and adds nothing.",
   "Step 5: the windscreen is assumed to clutch the 2x2 plate and two 1x2 plates, with the hinge stack behind it. The 2x2 tile with top pin goes on the hinge top plate. The axle, angled connector and pin sub-assembly goes sideways through the Technic brick's axle hole.",
   "Step 6: the weapon (434926) and the camera (436026) are placed on the black 2x6 plate near the skids. Their exact attachment is hard to read, so this is a guess. Their clips are not modelled.",
   "Piece count across both pages is 26, which matches the parts list. The minifigure is not in the parts list."
